    {
      "calls": [
        {
          "ID": "toolu_01RuWBKnRSFw1HLuWJR9o3j4",
          "Name": "submit_read",
          "Input": {
            "assessments": [
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13",
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S3:F33"
                ],
                "ref": "N1",
                "statement": "The UK is backing the US-announced energy ceasefire while tightening economic pressure on Russia, so a ceasefire that still has no start date has not softened UK policy, and sanctions are running alongside the diplomacy as leverage rather than being paused for it.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F39",
                  "S2:F40",
                  "S2:F33",
                  "S2:F45"
                ],
                "ref": "N2",
                "statement": "The week's new UK military aid to Ukraine is mostly about speeding up what was already promised, bringing forward £10m of a £45m missile package; the larger new sanctions, military and fiscal packages have been commissioned but not yet set out.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S16:F93",
                  "S16:F73",
                  "S10:F50",
                  "S10:F55",
                  "S14:F56",
                  "S16:F86"
                ],
                "ref": "N3",
                "statement": "The government's domestic announcements this week share one theme, moving government and spending out of London: Number 10 North, Great British Railways' headquarters and new trains in Derby, and an offer to devolve employment support to Scotland.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S16:F72",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F92",
                  "S16:F83",
                  "S17:F82"
                ],
                "ref": "N4",
                "statement": "The Prime Minister's offer to Holyrood is so far mostly stated intent; the matched college funding shows cooperation working on a small scale, and the first real test is the National Economic Council meeting with the First Ministers, due a couple of weeks after 16 October.",
                "supersedes": ""
              }
            ],
            "statements": [
              {
                "cites": [
                  "L1",
                  "L2"
                ],
                "text": "Andy Burnham has been Prime Minister since 20 July 2026, after nine years as Mayor of Greater Manchester. This week almost every Story moved on the back of a run of his government's statements between 12 and 16 October."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13"
                ],
                "text": "On Russia, President Trump announced a reciprocal energy ceasefire, and Ukraine says it will implement it straight away once a start date is confirmed. The Record has no start date yet."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S3:F33"
                ],
                "text": "In the same days the UK went further on pressure. It announced a sanctions package covering over 90% of Russia's oil-producing capacity, committed to fully implementing a maritime services ban on Russian LNG, and had ministers draw up still more sanctions."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "N1"
                ],
                "text": "Read together, the ceasefire has not softened London's line. The UK is running sanctions alongside the diplomacy as leverage, not pausing them for it."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40",
                  "S2:F39",
                  "S2:F33",
                  "N2"
                ],
                "text": "The military side was more modest than the headlines. The UK is bringing forward £10m of a £45m surface-to-air missile package and speeding up Lightweight Multirole Missile deliveries. The bigger new military and fiscal packages have been commissioned but not yet set out."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S16:F93",
                  "S10:F50",
                  "S10:F55",
                  "S14:F56",
                  "S16:F86"
                ],
                "text": "At home the announcements pointed one way. The Prime Minister has set up Number 10 North. Great British Railways' headquarters, for up to 450 staff, was unveiled in Derby, where a £1bn fleet of new trains for the north is to be built at Alstom's site. Scotland has been offered devolution of DWP employment support."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "N3",
                  "L2"
                ],
                "text": "The common thread is moving government and spending out of London. That fits a Prime Minister who came to No 10 from a regional mayoralty."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S17:F82",
                  "S16:F83",
                  "N4"
                ],
                "text": "The offer to Holyrood is still mostly stated intent. The Scottish Government matching £10m for two defence technical colleges shows cooperation working on a small scale. The first real test is the National Economic Council meeting with the First Ministers of Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland, due a couple of weeks after 16 October."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S8:F27",
                  "S8:F85"
                ],
                "text": "Further ahead, the Prime Minister chose his Scotland speech to say he will seek a new food and farming deal at the UK-EU summit in Brussels on 20 November. That is the next dated point where this week's promises meet an outcome."
              }
            ],
            "stories": []
          }
        }
      ],
