                {
                  "cites": [
                    "S2:F34",
                    "S2:F40",
                    "S2:F39",
                    "S2:F33",
                    "N2"
                  ],
                  "text": "The military side was more modest than the headlines. The UK is bringing forward £10m of a £45m surface-to-air missile package and speeding up Lightweight Multirole Missile deliveries. The bigger new military and fiscal packages have been commissioned but not yet set out."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "S16:F93",
                    "S10:F50",
                    "S10:F55",
                    "S14:F56",
                    "S16:F86"
                  ],
                  "text": "At home the announcements pointed one way. The Prime Minister has set up Number 10 North. Great British Railways' headquarters, for up to 450 staff, was unveiled in Derby, where a £1bn fleet of new trains for the north is to be built at Alstom's site. Scotland has been offered devolution of DWP employment support."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "N3",
                    "L2"
                  ],
                  "text": "The common thread is moving government and spending out of London. That fits a Prime Minister who came to No 10 from a regional mayoralty."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "S17:F82",
                    "S16:F83",
                    "N4"
                  ],
                  "text": "The offer to Holyrood is still mostly stated intent. The Scottish Government matching £10m for two defence technical colleges shows cooperation working on a small scale. The first real test is the National Economic Council meeting with the First Ministers of Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland, due a couple of weeks after 16 October."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "S8:F27",
                    "S8:F85"
                  ],
                  "text": "Further ahead, the Prime Minister chose his Scotland speech to say he will seek a new food and farming deal at the UK-EU summit in Brussels on 20 November. That is the next dated point where this week's promises meet an outcome."
                }
              ],
              "stories": []
            },
